    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Vertical joint sets in Entrada Sandstone on the NW limb of Salt Valley anticline show abrupt changes in strike of up to 35°. Within the Moab member there are three areas of different joint orientations. Joints in northern and southern areas are older than the central area. Joints in the underlying Slick Rock member nucleate from breakdown fringes along joints in the Moab member, and change strike as much as 35°from joints in the Moab member. Joints in all areas are almost vertical, and do not change orientation as the attitude of bedding changes.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
